#: ../../identity-provider.rst:9
msgid "Keycloak as identity provider for ASM"
msgstr ""

#: ../../identity-provider.rst:11
msgid ""
"Apple School Manager can federate the sign-in of its Managed Apple "
"Accounts to an external identity provider. Your users then sign in to "
"their Apple devices with the password from your UCS\\@school domain "
"instead of a password that Apple School Manager manages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../identity-provider.rst:17
msgid ""
"This chapter describes how to set up the :term:`Keycloak` app of "
":term:`UCS` as that identity provider."
msgstr ""

#: ../../identity-provider.rst:22
msgid ""
"The :term:`SSF` support that Apple School Manager requires is an "
"experimental feature of Keycloak. Univention doesn't support this setup "
"in production yet. Try it in a test environment first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../identity-provider.rst:30
msgid "Why Apple School Manager needs SSF"
msgstr ""

#: ../../identity-provider.rst:32
msgid ""
"The Shared Signals Framework is the standard of the OpenID Foundation for"
" sharing security events, state changes, and risk signals between an "
"identity provider and the applications that rely on it. See :cite:t"
":`openid-ssf`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../identity-provider.rst:37
msgid ""
"Apple School Manager uses SSF to learn about events in your domain, such "
"as a changed credential or a revoked session. It therefore only accepts "
"an identity provider that acts as an SSF transmitter. A plain "
":term:`OIDC` client isn't enough."
msgstr ""

#: ../../identity-provider.rst:45
msgid "What you need"
msgstr ""

#: ../../identity-provider.rst:47
msgid ""
"A UCS\\@school domain with the Apple School Manager Connector and the "
"Keycloak app in version ``26.7.1`` or later."
msgstr ""

#: ../../identity-provider.rst:51
msgid ""
"A domain that you verified in Apple School Manager. See :cite:t:`apple-"
"verify-domain`. Your users need a primary email address in that domain to"
" sign in."
msgstr ""

